  "id": "independent-samples",
  "term": "independent samples",
  "definition": "Independent samples are separate groups of observations in which each person contributes data to only one group, such as one group rating one movie and a different group rating another. In research methods, this contrasts with correlated or dependent samples, where the same participants provide data in both conditions.",
